+### Persistent Octree (POT)
+A compact 3D or 4D octree that stores active cells for all isosurfaces, treating time as a spatial dimension [S3]. It extracts all cells that contain the isovalue and intersect a temporal hyperplane [S3]. It exhibits slightly quicker rendering times than BONO but has significant memory overhead [S3].
+
+### Video Metaphor with Modified THIT
+A technique using the video metaphor and a modified THIT to efficiently encode the difference between time steps, enabling quick random access through key frames [S3]. It places key frames appropriately to enable quick random access into the dataset [S3].
+
+### Out-of-core THIT
+An out-of-core variation of THIT used to quickly render approximate isosurfaces, addressing the bottleneck of accessing field values from disk [S3]. It develops a point splatting algorithm that uses only the min-max range of a cell to render approximate isosurfaces [S3].
+
